/**
 *
 *  JournalEntries.h
 *
 *  Hand-authored, drogon_ctl-shape-compatible model for `journal_entries`.
 *  Originally generated by drogon_ctl against the V001 baseline schema
 *  (31 columns). V003__phase3_ledger.sql (Phase 3) appends three columns
 *  used for the tamper-evident hash chain described in the implementation
 *  plan's Ledger correctness rules:
 *    - entry_seq   bigserial  — per-tenant monotonic ordering for the chain
 *                               (the uuid primary key is not chronologically
 *                               sortable, so hashing needs its own sequence)
 *    - entry_hash  varchar(64) — sha256(prev_hash || canonical entry fields)
 *    - prev_hash   varchar(64) — the previous entry's hash in this tenant's
 *                               chain (null for the first entry)
 *  This sandbox has no live Postgres to re-run `drogon_ctl create_model`
 *  against, so the three new columns were added by hand, in place, in every
 *  spot the generator would touch for a real column of that type — see
 *  JournalService.cc for the only two writers (hash chaining happens once,
 *  at insert time; entries are otherwise immutable).
 *
 *  As with the Phase 2 hand-authored models, the JSON (de)serialization
 *  surface that a live drogon_ctl would also emit (toJson/toMasqueradedJson,
 *  the two Json::Value constructors, updateByJson/updateByMasqueradedJson,
 *  validateJsonForCreation/validateMasqueradedJsonForCreation/
 *  validateJsonForUpdate/validateMasqueradedJsonForUpdate/validJsonOfField)
 *  is intentionally omitted: nothing in this codebase calls it — JSON in/out
 *  is handled explicitly by JournalService, matching every other Accounting
 *  and Organization model. Regenerate for real if a future feature needs it.
 *
 */

